Subject: [sshmap fork 0013] the erase family's SECOND half — `CSI 3 J` keeps the visible grid and an erased cell keeps only the colours

Provenance: sshmap (v1.9.3, ROADMAP task 1) — item (c) of the three pyte cosmetics the dependency audit
            left in the backlog (PYTE82_AUDIT.md, the raise-review of 2026-09-26, "the two neighbours of
            that same erase family"): the two hunks patch 0012 deliberately left alone, measured on the
            vendored fork first. (i) `erase_in_display` answered `how == 3` with the SAME
            `range(self.lines)` interval as `2`, so `CSI 3 J` also wiped the VISIBLE screen where xterm
            clears the SAVED lines only — measured: `ESC[3J` on a written 3-line screen blanked every
            visible row, while the mode's documented meaning is the scrollback. A plain `Screen` keeps no
            saved lines at all, so the honest reading there is the NO-OP branch `erase_in_line` already
            takes for a mode it does not implement, and `HistoryScreen._reset_history()` stays the whole
            effect of the mode where the saved lines exist. (ii) `_erase_attrs()` handed an erased cell
            `self.cursor.attrs` WHOLE, so `underscore` — and every other glyph decoration — survived an
            erase; the canvas paints the underline of a run of SPACES too (`QFont.setUnderline` plus
            `drawText(" ")`), which is the recorded symptom of a line drawn across the blank area.
            xterm's BCE takes the current BACKGROUND and colours, not the decoration of a glyph that is
            no longer there.
            The decision the patch carries: what an erased cell KEEPS is ONE declared set — the COLOURS
            (fg, bg and the DECSCNM/SGR-7 reverse) — so `_erase_attrs()` is the single place that
            answers it and the three erase paths (`erase_characters`, `erase_in_line`,
            `erase_in_display`) cannot drift. Also measured, on the vendored fork: the visible grid of
            both screens really does survive `ESC[3J` after the patch (0 of 15 cells rewritten on a
            30x5 written row, against 15 of 15 before it) while the scrollback is still dropped.
Base:       pyte 0.8.2 (PyPI sdist, sha256 in MANIFEST.md), pyte/screens.py (after patches
            0001-0012; patch 0012 was the last one to touch this file).
Policy:     keep — 0.8.3.dev carries BOTH shapes (the `2 or 3` branch and the whole-attrs erase), so
            there is no release to wait for; each hunk is additive to the helper and to one branch, so
            a future rebase can re-apply it alone.
Applied:    2026-10-08, sshmap v1.9.3.

diff --git a/pyte/screens.py b/pyte/screens.py
